  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bromobenzene is treated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>conc</mi><mo>.</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>, 4, 6 </mo><mi>trinitrophenol</mi></math> by electrophilic substitution reaction mechanism, which on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> give trinitrophenol. It is also known as picric acid.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0037_7179f5be6ac3.png\" style=\"width: 734px; height: 451px;\"/></p>"
